						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														I had a talk with Nam and some of my friends and after they get to certain stage of buying armour I've agreed with them that it takes too long, and too much money. I play EverQuest to try new things, and to have some fun, not to sit around in bazaar all day typing WTS WTB WTT etc. So I came to this conclusion -<br />
<br />
If everyone wants to, we could start hunting in Kael arena for Corroded armour drops ( and caster armour drops ) and helping eachother get the quests done. Breastplates and robes would maybe take a little while longer to do, we'd need a high end group for the Velk's castle or the Kobold camp in Velk's.<br />
I know we're not a raiding guild, but this isn't really raiding, just helping eachother out :) The armour is really nice, and once you have the corroded piece, the gems are normally on sale in Bazaar for 50pp or so, and can be easily obtained with a steady group in Velk's lab.<br />
<br />
I'm open to suggestions on this, give me some feedback :)<br />
<br />
Example of the kind of armour you get from the quests... the paladin breastplate is called &quot;Runed Protector's Breastplate&quot;.. it has Shield of Words as a manaless cast.. and 47ac + some nice stats.. so I can only think the other armour would be similiar for different classes.<br />
<br />
As I said, I'm looking for this to be a guild activity, if we could get some active and willing 50+ players online at the same time, this could be very possible. <br />
<br />
Edit : oops cleric bp doesn't have complete heal, that's Donal's chestplate of mourning, a kunark dragon dropped bp, not the velious quested ones. oops, again.						</td>
